IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `ei2-nouns`

-- Employment Insurance Act (S.C. 1996, c. 23), ss 24 to 26: work-sharing; courses, programs and employment
-- support measures; benefits that are not earnings. Piece ei2. Text: the unofficial plain-text rendering of
-- the Justice Laws consolidation current to 2026-09-30. Seat: the claimant.
--
-- WHAT KIND OF ANSWER A DEEMING RULE GIVES. Sections 24(3), 25(1) and 26 say that in a stated case a claimant IS
-- treated in a stated way. They do not say that outside that case the claimant is NOT: other provisions decide
-- that. So each returns MAYBE BOOLEAN: JUST TRUE when the provision applies, NOTHING when it does not, and never
-- FALSE. (The keel does the same for the open definition of "documents".) The seat layer words its question so
-- that FALSE means "this provision does not apply", not "the opposite is true".
--
-- A "no appeal" rule (ss 24(2), 25(2)) is the same: JUST TRUE when the decision is of the described kind and so
-- cannot be reviewed under s 112 (the review itself is s 112, piece ei4); NOTHING when it is some other decision,
-- about which these sections say nothing.
--
-- Section 24(1) (regulations for work-sharing benefits) is a regulation-making power: inert machinery, see the
-- coverage table in NOTES.md. Regs 42 to 49 (piece er3) are the regulations made under it.

§ `Section 24 - work-sharing`

-- s 24(2): a direction approving or disapproving a work-sharing agreement is closed to review under s 112 (out of
-- range: section 112, piece ei4). The person bound is any claimant or employer whose agreement the Commission
-- approves or disapproves: they lose the power to ask for reconsideration (a disability); the Commission's
-- direction is immune from review (an immunity). Its disability and the person's liability are the same relation.
-- src:691 | No appeal
-- src:692 | (2) A special or general direction of the Commission approving or disapproving a work sharing agreement for the purposes of subsection (1) is not subject to review under section 112.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 24(2) (src:691-692)
GIVEN `the decision is a special or general direction of the Commission approving or disapproving a work sharing agreement for the purposes of subsection 24(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 24(2) the direction on a work sharing agreement is not subject to review under section 112` IS
    IF `the decision is a special or general direction of the Commission approving or disapproving a work sharing agreement for the purposes of subsection 24(1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 24(3): what work-sharing employment is, is for the regulations (24(1)(a); regs 42 to 49, piece er3); here it is
-- the one fact "works in work-sharing employment during the week".
-- src:693 | Presumption
-- src:694 | (3) For the purposes of this Part, a claimant is unemployed and capable of and available for work during a week when the claimant works in work-sharing employment.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 24(3) (src:693-694)
GIVEN `the claimant works in work-sharing employment during the week` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 24(3) the claimant is unemployed and capable of and available for work during the week` IS
    IF `the claimant works in work-sharing employment during the week`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 25 - courses, programs and employment support measures`

-- The kind of employment support measure (s 59) is a MAYBE here because a course or an activity may be under no
-- measure at all (at the claimant's own expense, or under a measure that is the subject of an agreement under s 63).
-- The helpers below read it.
-- src:1072 | 59 The Commission may establish employment support measures to help insured participants and other workers, including workers in groups underrepresented in the labour market, to obtain or keep employment, including measures to
-- src:1073 | (a) provide insured participants with courses or programs of instruction or training;
-- src:1074 | (b) provide insured participants with employment opportunities or provide employment support;
-- src:1075 | (c) provide workers with employment assistance services; and
-- src:1076 | (d) support research, innovation or partnerships related to helping workers to prepare for, obtain or keep employment and to be productive participants in the labour market.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 59 (src:1072-1076)
GIVEN `the measure, if there is one` IS A MAYBE `ei2 Kind of employment support measure`
      `the kind` IS A `ei2 Kind of employment support measure`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `ei2 s 59 the measure is of the kind` IS
    CONSIDER `the measure, if there is one`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST k  THEN k EQUALS `the kind`

-- "an employment support measure ... other than one referred to in paragraph 59(c) or (d)" (ss 26, 5(1)(e)); the words "other than" qualify the
-- employment support measure and not a measure that is the subject of a section 63 agreement (fork ei2-F15). And
-- "other than one referred to in paragraph 59(a) or (c)" (s 25(1)(b)(i)): there is a measure and it is none of the two.
-- src:1072 | 59 The Commission may establish employment support measures to help insured participants and other workers, including workers in groups underrepresented in the labour market, to obtain or keep employment, including measures to
-- src:1073 | (a) provide insured participants with courses or programs of instruction or training;
-- src:1074 | (b) provide insured participants with employment opportunities or provide employment support;
-- src:1075 | (c) provide workers with employment assistance services; and
-- src:1076 | (d) support research, innovation or partnerships related to helping workers to prepare for, obtain or keep employment and to be productive participants in the labour market.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 59 (src:1072-1076)
GIVEN `the measure, if there is one` IS A MAYBE `ei2 Kind of employment support measure`
      `the first kind excluded` IS A `ei2 Kind of employment support measure`
      `the second kind excluded` IS A `ei2 Kind of employment support measure`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `ei2 s 59 there is a measure and it is of neither of the two kinds` IS
    CONSIDER `the measure, if there is one`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST k  THEN (NOT (k EQUALS `the first kind excluded`)) AND (NOT (k EQUALS `the second kind excluded`))

-- "an employment support measure ... other than one referred to in paragraph 59(c)" (s 27(1.1)(a)): there is a
-- measure and it is not of that one kind.
-- src:1072 | 59 The Commission may establish employment support measures to help insured participants and other workers, including workers in groups underrepresented in the labour market, to obtain or keep employment, including measures to
-- src:1073 | (a) provide insured participants with courses or programs of instruction or training;
-- src:1074 | (b) provide insured participants with employment opportunities or provide employment support;
-- src:1075 | (c) provide workers with employment assistance services; and
-- src:1076 | (d) support research, innovation or partnerships related to helping workers to prepare for, obtain or keep employment and to be productive participants in the labour market.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 59 (src:1072-1076)
GIVEN `the measure, if there is one` IS A MAYBE `ei2 Kind of employment support measure`
      `the kind excluded` IS A `ei2 Kind of employment support measure`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `ei2 s 59 there is a measure and it is not of the kind` IS
    CONSIDER `the measure, if there is one`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST k  THEN NOT (k EQUALS `the kind excluded`)

-- 25(1)(a): "attending a course or program of instruction or training -- at the claimant's own expense, under an
-- employment support measure referred to in paragraph 59(a) or under a measure that is the subject of an agreement
-- under section 63 -- to which the Commission, or an authority that the Commission designates, has referred the claimant".
-- src:698 | 25 (1) For the purposes of this Part, a claimant is unemployed and capable of and available for work during a period when the claimant is
-- src:699 | (a) attending a course or program of instruction or training — at the claimant’s own expense, under an employment support measure referred to in paragraph 59(a) or under a measure that is the subject of an agreement under section 63 — to which the Commission, or an authority that the Commission designates, has referred the claimant; or
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 25(1)(a) (src:698-699)
GIVEN `attending a course or program of instruction or training` IS A BOOLEAN
      `at the claimant's own expense` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employment support measure under which the course or program is given, if any` IS A MAYBE `ei2 Kind of employment support measure`
      `under a measure that is the subject of an agreement under section 63` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commission, or an authority that the Commission designates, has referred the claimant to it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 25(1)(a) attending a referred course or program of instruction or training` IF
        `attending a course or program of instruction or training`
    AND (   `at the claimant's own expense`
         OR `ei2 s 59 the measure is of the kind` `the employment support measure under which the course or program is given, if any` `ei2 s 59(a) measure providing courses or programs of instruction or training`
         OR `under a measure that is the subject of an agreement under section 63`)
    AND `the Commission, or an authority that the Commission designates, has referred the claimant to it`

-- 25(1)(b): "participating in any other employment activity (i) for which assistance has been provided for the claimant
-- under a prescribed employment support measure -- other than one referred to in paragraph 59(a) or (c) -- or a
-- prescribed measure that is the subject of an agreement under section 63, and (ii) to which the Commission, or an
-- authority that the Commission designates, has referred the claimant." Which measures are prescribed is reg 50
-- (out of range: Regulations s 50, piece er3): it is the BOOLEAN input "is prescribed".
-- src:700 | (b) participating in any other employment activity
-- src:701 | (i) for which assistance has been provided for the claimant under a prescribed employment support measure — other than one referred to in paragraph 59(a) or (c) — or a prescribed measure that is the subject of an agreement under section 63, and
-- src:702 | (ii) to which the Commission, or an authority that the Commission designates, has referred the claimant.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 25(1)(b) (src:700-702)
GIVEN `participating in any other employment activity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employment support measure under which assistance has been provided for the claimant, if any` IS A MAYBE `ei2 Kind of employment support measure`
      `that measure is prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `assistance has been provided under a prescribed measure that is the subject of an agreement under section 63` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commission, or an authority that the Commission designates, has referred the claimant to the activity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 25(1)(b) participating in a referred employment activity` IF
        `participating in any other employment activity`
    AND (   (    `ei2 s 59 there is a measure and it is of neither of the two kinds` `the employment support measure under which assistance has been provided for the claimant, if any` `ei2 s 59(a) measure providing courses or programs of instruction or training` `ei2 s 59(c) measure providing employment assistance services`
             AND `that measure is prescribed`)
         OR `assistance has been provided under a prescribed measure that is the subject of an agreement under section 63`)
    AND `the Commission, or an authority that the Commission designates, has referred the claimant to the activity`

-- src:698 | 25 (1) For the purposes of this Part, a claimant is unemployed and capable of and available for work during a period when the claimant is
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 25(1) (src:698)
GIVEN `attending a referred course or program of instruction or training` IS A BOOLEAN
      `participating in a referred employment activity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 25(1) the claimant is unemployed and capable of and available for work during the period` IS
    IF `attending a referred course or program of instruction or training` OR `participating in a referred employment activity`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 25(2): the decision about the referral cannot be reviewed under s 112 (out of range: section 112, piece ei4).
-- src:703 | No appeal
-- src:704 | (2) A decision of the Commission about the referral of a claimant to a course, program or other employment activity mentioned in subsection (1) is not subject to review under section 112.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 25(2) (src:703-704)
GIVEN `the decision is a decision of the Commission about the referral of a claimant to a course, program or other employment activity mentioned in subsection 25(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 25(2) the decision about the referral is not subject to review under section 112` IS
    IF `the decision is a decision of the Commission about the referral of a claimant to a course, program or other employment activity mentioned in subsection 25(1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 26 - benefits are not earnings`

-- "For the purposes of this Part, Part IV, the Income Tax Act and the Canada Pension Plan, benefits paid to a claimant
-- while employed under an employment support measure -- other than one referred to in paragraph 59(c) or (d) -- or
-- under a measure that is the subject of an agreement under section 63 are not earnings from employment."
-- src:705 | Benefits are not earnings
-- src:706 | 26 For the purposes of this Part, Part IV, the Income Tax Act and the Canada Pension Plan, benefits paid to a claimant while employed under an employment support measure — other than one referred to in paragraph 59(c) or (d) — or under a measure that is the subject of an agreement under section 63 are not earnings from employment.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 26 (src:705-706)
GIVEN `benefits are paid to the claimant while employed under an employment support measure or a measure that is the subject of an agreement under section 63` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employment support measure the claimant is employed under, if any` IS A MAYBE `ei2 Kind of employment support measure`
      `the claimant is employed under a measure that is the subject of an agreement under section 63` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 26 the benefits paid are not earnings from employment` IS
    IF     `benefits are paid to the claimant while employed under an employment support measure or a measure that is the subject of an agreement under section 63`
       AND (   `ei2 s 59 there is a measure and it is of neither of the two kinds` `the employment support measure the claimant is employed under, if any` `ei2 s 59(c) measure providing employment assistance services` `ei2 s 59(d) measure supporting research, innovation or partnerships`
            OR `the claimant is employed under a measure that is the subject of an agreement under section 63`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING
